  "description": "\"The wild pear that didn't ripen in summer—that child walks in.\" \n\nTwenty-one-year-old Bae Gong-ju has never left her small village. One day, a new boxing gym opens in town, and when she goes to sneak a peek, a handsome man she’s never seen before approaches her. \n\n\"Want to grab a cup of coffee? Let’s go to a cafe.\" \n\nHaving worked in the pear orchards among elderly women since she was young, Gong-ju never had many opportunities to mingle with others, and this strange man’s sudden approach feels surreal. Although his strangely intrusive demeanor feels awkward, a corner of her heart keeps fluttering. Since that day, Cheon-yeok has been visiting the pear orchard every day, slowly seeping into Gong-ju's familiar routine... His nonchalant yet affectionate gestures, his unhesitating gaze, and an attraction that is hard to explain. \n\nA strange encounter that began in the sweltering heat of summer. How far will the relationship between these two, as clumsy as an unripened pear, eventually ripen?\n\n[Original Webtoon](https://series.naver.com/comic/detail.series?productNo=14442664)",
